{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0ec3dce3e6975952bc76929740b1b306f48f4d04d2f0ae813b4bdca3c8a41b6c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An integrated terminal is documented with cross-platform support, xterm.js integration, real-time output streaming, command history, and native shells (cmd.exe on Windows, bash on Linux)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_10097a35fadb6844c554c1e28507912a26242dae737bb94b3464457004c84c6f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the README invites contributions via pull requests."},{"claim_ids":["clm_156902ea77f1d0d160b7e6fce4fda19ea389a5d56d59e1d84dcf49372f8ac15f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The frontend is documented as pure JavaScript with TailwindCSS, CodeMirror, Socket.IO client, PDF.js, Mammoth.js, XLSX.js, Tesseract.js, and Marked/Unified.js."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3dbb5a2b9ea18f2fd6b6d14eca04665097fbd94c550298c77ea39b9e660f6a98"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Code generation features include generating code from natural-language prompts, modifying existing code, previewing changes, and viewing diffs before applying."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5f59c8fe2fdaf7d528abcbed132a64de26137ffcf5f0521a5ec1667a95bdedd1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Setup involves pip-installing requirements.txt and setting .env API keys for DeepSeek, Codestral, OpenRouter, Google, Grok, Anthropic, and OpenAI."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5fb462fa8f95119daac248f0641bdf9d42def79cee4473b1817d58fd351c853e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The app is started with 'python app.py' and accessed at http://localhost:5000, where users create or select a workspace and choose an AI model."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8d8dc2c11c536e151873b7bdb3651d5fc3b690f86b0245d3ff65bf8300ed90b4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The app is documented as tested on Linux, WSL 2, and native Windows, using directory junctions on Windows to avoid requiring admin privileges."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9915fa9fb4220a1dd280a882cd255b6b0daa2f775df44163d4ad59d5c2ba9ebc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Workspace management lets users create, rename, and delete multiple workspaces, view workspace history, and browse the workspace file structure."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a3003c1dace6fd341fc5b152539173f444818522c1821627e847ae17a5e80236"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Real-time updates are delivered via WebSocket-based notifications for code changes and workspace updates."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b1021e1226d838f4ffc5421db7a79c332e80cd14e545bbf36cd662fa45f76891"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product offers selectable AI models including DeepSeek R1/V3, Codestral, Gemini 2.0 Flash Experimental, Grok 2, Claude 3.5 Sonnet, GPT-4 Turbo, GPT-4o variants, and o1 models."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bb5673640078c1b80868b8530f71dd249e815d3a20b0f2229761219a73ce8f77"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The backend is documented as using the Flask web framework, Flask-SocketIO for WebSocket support, and Eventlet for async operations."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ef372a72b2a0b8bc058ff90584b77958fcb389c8c9f583d397c72a282447f3fd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"J.A.R.V.I.S. is described as an AI coding assistant leveraging multiple state-of-the-art language models for code generation, modification, and technical discussions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f745b5cac16baae219ea759375e38641e4bb38365e692469a4417ae1ab6d1bcb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"File attachment support covers PDFs with text extraction, .docx, Excel parsing, image OCR, Markdown with GFM, code and config files, with previews and multiple uploads."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0ec3dce3e6975952bc76929740b1b306f48f4d04d2f0ae813b4bdca3c8a41b6c","clm_10097a35fadb6844c554c1e28507912a26242dae737bb94b3464457004c84c6f","clm_156902ea77f1d0d160b7e6fce4fda19ea389a5d56d59e1d84dcf49372f8ac15f","clm_3dbb5a2b9ea18f2fd6b6d14eca04665097fbd94c550298c77ea39b9e660f6a98","clm_5f59c8fe2fdaf7d528abcbed132a64de26137ffcf5f0521a5ec1667a95bdedd1","clm_5fb462fa8f95119daac248f0641bdf9d42def79cee4473b1817d58fd351c853e","clm_8d8dc2c11c536e151873b7